Give Position and Location their drake surfaces and the generator's companions

Dev accepted, in these words: "Accepted, build it" — the recommendation being that aerial Position
and terrestrial Location, the two coordinate types of the example chain, take their drake surfaces
as the emitter writes them, have their hand-written companions replaced by the generator's output,
and gain one CoordinateProjectionTest in the domains package iterating over the two: trio agreement,
lazy defaults and Null, the codec round-trip with missing-field defaults.

Why these two: of the eleven example differences the generate map reported after 3a3cbfc, nine are
companion spelling (`with DracoType`, `override`, imports, Input's actor convention); Position and
Location were the two whose companions lacked something the definition carries — the codec the
generator infers from three fixed elements with defaulted factory parameters, exactly the gap
Cartesian closed on 2026-10-25 when its inferred coordinate codecs were accepted. Neither had a
drake surface.

Probed before recommending, with the compiled CLIs: `DrakeCLI emit` renders each surface from its
JSON — `type Position from Aerial`, three `fix` elements, `factory parameters` with three defaulted
`par` lines, the domain line — and parsing it back reproduces the committed JSON byte for byte, so
the JSON does not move; the generator's companion differs from the hand-written one only by the
inferred codec, 21 lines: `implicit lazy val encoder` writing the three fields by name, `implicit
lazy val decoder` reading each through `Option` with the factory default for a missing field, and
the imports `domains._`, `io.circe.{Decoder, Encoder, Json}`, `io.circe.syntax.EncoderOps`. Trait,
loader line, kind-vals, `apply` and `Null` are unchanged, so every caller — Input's Position
construction, world Consumer's Location construction, five tests — is untouched. Built as probed:
two surfaces placed from the emitter's rendering, two companions regenerated, `DrakeCLI check`
over aerial and terrestrial: surface drift 0, json drift 0. No engine change, no JSON change.

CoordinateProjectionTest (3) is one suite, each case iterating over the two: exact trio agreement
(emit, parse, generate, the three element names, the three factory defaults, the companion's
loaded definition equal to the file's); the factory's arguments lazy and evaluated once on first
read, Null and an omitted argument at zero; and the inferred codec writing the three fields by name,
reading them back onto the companion's definition, decoding an empty object to the three defaults,
a lone third field to the defaults plus that field, and refusing an invalid latitude.

